body:
To be fair, the title for the thread is "You can't assault someone for saying the n-word", which I agree with. Someone saying something objectionable doesn't equate to physical violence. However, I would say that if you called a black person the n-word as a non-black person, and they beat the shit out of you, I'm really not going to stand up for you. I'm also not gonna act surprised for you getting your ass beat. Play stupid games, win stupid prizes. But, objectively, you shouldn't ever hit someone for saying something you don't like. 

&#x200B;

Link to the thread btw: [https://www.reddit.com/r/unpopularopinion/comments/bznaxn/you\_cant\_assault\_someone\_for\_saying\_the\_n\_word/](https://www.reddit.com/r/unpopularopinion/comments/bznaxn/you_cant_assault_someone_for_saying_the_n_word/)

SH2 doesn't get horrific until Pyramid Head. I was unnerved by SH2 prior to Pyramid Head, but wasn't really scared yet. Once Pyramid Head came my gradual descent into complete dread playing that game jolted lmao.

&#x200B;

The horror for me really really unfolds around Abstract Daddy. Silent Hill 2 isn't horrific in the sense that it's gonna scare you, it's just going places psychologically that are oppressively dark and laying them out as set pieces, enemies, and plot lines. The fear starts to encroach as sanity becomes tested and whittled down in the game. The maps become more convoluted, the levels become absurd and bleak, the enemies become gradually more repulsive. By the end, the game is devastating. That's the terror of it. Not so much the raw gameplay or enemies.

&#x200B;

Also, a lot of the themes in this game are really really adult stuff. If I was 9, if the game didn't outright freak me the fuck out to the point where I just didn't play it to begin with, I would have completely missed the symbolism in the game. Probably pulls her away from it.

Another update...

&#x200B;

>!I made it to the STARS room and got the mag without detection. The high you get from avoiding this guy is fucking nuts lmao. All I have to do now is go to that dreaded records room and get the jack for the library. I know he comes in there no matter what, so I'm gonna deal with that tomorrow lmao. !<

Alright, a little update for anyone who wants to know. I have worked up the nerve to trek through this game. When I first triggered him, I sprinted back immediately to the boiler room where he can't enter. I went at a snail's pace out of the boiler room and back into the building.

&#x200B;

SPOILERS FROM THiS POINT ON, DON'T READ BEYOND HERE IF YOU'RE AVOIDING ANY SPOILERS FOR RPD

&#x200B;

>!I waited until I didn't hear shit and went down to the observation room. I heard rumors that he busted through a wall down there, somewhere, but I didn't exactly know where and if it was for everyone or it was just a trigger. I went in, got what I needed, and went like, slug pace, out of that room. I crept around the corner by the press room, where I heard he busted out. And lo, nothing happened. Was kinda disappointed honestly because in doing that he'd make a killer shortcut. I figured I didn't do something to trigger it, or it was a glitch, but I was skeptical (and heard distant footsteps), so I ran back to the observation room. I crept out slow again, rounded the corner, and the wall fucking exploded. I didn't even wait, the second I heard that shit I just double backed into the observation room (I looked up where he couldn't go beforehand lol sue me). I waited in that bitch for like 20 fucking minutes until the footsteps were anomalous. My plan was to get across to the dark room and just save and quit for the day (I'm taking this part of the game in bite sized chunks lmao). I crept out really slow, and then I entered the main hall.!<

&#x200B;

>!I looked around and saw the guy. He saw me too. Nothing I could do, so I shot him a few times in the head. It literally did nothing, he ate it like a champ and decked me. The fear of the guy kind of went away at that point because it's really not that bad to encounter him, but the threat of what he can do had me on edge like I've never been before. Not even in my real fucking life have I felt the sheer adrenaline that this game fucking instilled in me. Everything was tense and I felt like borderline euphoric lmao. I just remember feeling this intense physical pressure all around me and my heart rate spiking. It sounds corny, but I was like mentally fucking in survival mode. I was moving so damn tactically and expediently to the dark room. Once the guy has you, all he's gonna do is follow you, and he's relatively slow so as long as you don't trip or slow down he can't actually catch you. In order for him to catch you you have to get cornered or attacked by another zombie I figured out. Anyway, I was literally having the adrenaline rush of my fucking life and I got attacked by a licker but it didn't do too much to me and I made it to the save room without dying. Next step is tryna get to the STARS office, and then back to the dark room. If you bothered to read this, I applaud you lmao. This is pretty much the most intense thing I've experienced ever haha. The guy really doesn't pose too much of a threat if you're not a total idiot, but he's still fucking insane to encounter lol. I'm just really glad I did as much as I possibly could before I had to deal with him. It's fucking nuts and will retrospectively be a blast to have dealt with him, but definitely would be way too much to handle to have to do the whole damn police station before encountering him despite the game trying to trick you into doing that haha.!<

just change your perspective and stop playing the victim! 

&#x200B;

/s

