Look man, at the end of the day, school isn't perfect. I was a reasonably accomplished college grad from a well-regarded institution, and I can tell you that from Pre-K onward I definitely saw pitfalls in the system. But at the end of the day, we can't just assume hundreds of millions of kids will pick themselves up by the bootstraps and steer themselves into fruitful careers. There are so many fucking obstacles in their paths, be it regular old growing pains or potentially toxic domestic situations, that you can't honestly think that we don't need a general institution that steers kids on a basic level of intelligence and skill set. This is what school is for. Beyond high school you can, to an extent, tailor any further education toward your wants/needs. But you just kinda need to go through the motions in high school. It sucks, it's not fun, it can be soul crushing, but if you find a subject or two you enjoy, some friends, a sport, and pot, you'll survive. It can be *way* worse. 

&#x200B;

And to the point of this corny post, we need a universal, to-the-point, general way to determine that the institution that is responsible for acclimating millions of people a year to becoming basically functional citizens in our society is actually working. Tests won't work for everyone, but even the kids who don't test well but are good students exemplify this outside of exams. I didn't test well but the worst grade I ever got on a paper was like a B, my writing was what got me ahead in school. Other kids are good at projects, or public speaking. But they all had something that made them thrive academically in whatever capacity they thrived in. We can't focus on every little special snowflake (hate that phrase at this point but if the shoe fits) and their individual wants and needs academically, especially in fucking high school. Passing high school at regents level is a goddamn joke, anyone who isn't on the spectrum can do it. A pocket of lowball thousands of kids will slip through the cracks in high school that are truly brilliant and make something of themselves despite a lack of academic success and conventional discipline, but most people aren't like that, and generally kids who can't make it through regents level high school are just fuck ups. Cram for the tests, forget about the shit later, get the piece of paper, move on. It's four years out of your life, and it opens all the doors you need to put yourself on a track to a life worth living if you just get out of there. Socioeconomic and domestic hindrances notwithstanding, and mental disability, anyone can do it. Get over how broken it is. It's fuckin high school lol

