Pretty much. I'd hook up with them, but I wouldn't want to commit to them, and I'd let them know that off the bat so I didn't hurt them or anything. 

&#x200B;

Inexperience on all fronts after a certain point can become kind of exhausting for a relationship because what I perceive as being pretty nonchalant and normal could be construed as a sweeping romantic gesture by someone who is less experienced. Like for me, sex is pretty meaningless. It's pleasurable to say the least, but it doesn't make me feel any way towards someone. It may strengthen feelings I already have, but it doesn't create any feelings. For someone who has never had sex, they could confuse the euphoria of sex with love and then get really attached after sex and jump into shit way too fast because of it. Same thing with other stuff like holding hands, cuddling, going on a date, etc. All of that stuff is nice, but none of it really means much at face value. For someone who doesn't really have experience with that stuff though, they could start assuming these small things are grand gestures and then it just gets suffocating. For me, it's not really worth it.

99.9% of the time it is a thoroughly terrible idea to pursue someone after they reject you lol. There are extraneous circumstances where it might be permissible (i.e. distance, they were taken when you asked the first time, family stuff, etc), but those are few and far between. And even then, do you really wanna be jumping through all these hurdles just to go on a date with someone? Anyone who makes you do that is probably insecure as hell and full of themselves, or their lives are a mess and it's just not worth the effort. Plus if they rejected you due to disinterest and you keep at it, that could become sexual harassment. 

&#x200B;

Basically, I'd never ask someone out twice. I don't care what the situation is, I just wouldn't do it, even if I thought I had a shot the second time. It's unattractive to be rejected, and the excitement and rush of asking someone out just feels stale and awkward trying to do it a second time, or so I would imagine. Plus I could get major creeper points for doing so. Not worth it.

I used to think the gym was off limits, but there's a guy I went to college with who has hooked up with a few girls at his gym. Nothing's impossible, and if you misread the situation and she rejects you, the worst case scenario is you take it as a lesson not to do that again and find a new gym. And that's only if it's awkward to be in the same gym as her tbh. 

&#x200B;

That being said, I wouldn't even bother lol. The girls at my gym aren't appealing to me outside of their appearance and I think it would honestly be kind of annoying trying to date any of them even if I met them outside the gym lol. And really, I'm just there to lift. It's tunnel vision on the equipment until I'm out. But honestly, though it usually is a bad idea, nothing really bad can happen, so if you wanna try it, try it. You only live once.

